// Depth-trip settle guard (aug05a katana divergence_000000): a
// growing-argument non-tail recursion must SETTLE at the call-depth
// guard in O(depth) — one trip, the delivered tainted bottom rides the
// unwind, every outer call misses on the tainted scrutinee. Under the
// A1 transient pool (abd4339a, REMOVED 851b3a12+) the settle re-ignited:
// spuriously-rebound parked sites primed clean-FIRED args and
// redescended — 2.9M shallow re-trips / >8x timeout where pre-pool
// settled in 513 dispatches. Root category: instance-id reuse broke the
// settle protocol's id-sterility assumption (reset-to-fresh ≠ fresh
// identity — design/interp_lazy_bind_cost.md, A1 post-mortem). This pin
// times out, loudly, if any future reuse mechanism breaks the settle.
{let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {m if m <= i64:0 => i64:1, m => i64:0 + f(n + f(n - i64:1))}; let v = f(i64:8); false}
